        // Wild crops: the ripe plant of a crop (crops.ron) gone wild, where its seeds are first
        // found. Biomes take them only by the `wild_crop` tag (not by habitat tags such as
        // `meadow`, which would bring them in wherever meadow flowers grow), Rare as a rule,
        // so with Tag("wild_crop", 0.4) a fitting biome has one in a few chunks, a few in a
        // chunk in a world that features the crop, and fewer where the climate or habitat
        // suits it less. Their habitat and comfort decide which grows
        // where: potatoes in the open, cabbages on banks, strawberries under trees, tomatoes
        // where it is warm, saffron where it is dry. The wild forms of wheat, carrot, chili
        // and moonbloom are above.
        (
            name: "wild_potato", block: "potato_crop", spread: Alone, habitat: Open, rarity: Rare, tags: ["wild_crop"],
            comfort: (temperature: (0.0, 18.0), moisture: (0.6, 1.8)), properties: (nutrition: 3.0),
